{{PageBanner|instinct img01 en.jpg}}
'''Talents''' (本能 ''Hon'nō'', '''Instincts''') are an upgrade mechanic implemented in the [[Version 8.0 Update]]. Once unlocked by clearing [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3, this mechanic allows players to unlock and develop a selection of (normally) five or six upgrades for certain [[True Form]] cats that are level 30 or above. As a companion mechanic to Talents, [[Talent Orbs]] were introduced in [[Version 9.7 Update|Version 9.7]] and grant units equipped with them increased offensive and/or defensive power against a trait of choice. An expansion to Talents - classified as Ultra Talents - was added in [[Version 12.1 Update|Version 12.1]], allowing certain [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cats]] to unlock one to three additional Talents and equip a second Talent Orb when they are upgraded to level 60 or above. [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]] further increased the limit of Ultra Talents to six.

==Introduction==
[[File:Talent 6.png|thumb|150px|NP Coin]]
:"''Exchange unneeded Cat Units for NP, then use your collected NP to unlock or upgrade new abilities (Talents) for a cat's True Form. Each True Form has a different set of Talents that can be unlocked."'' - In-game description
Unlocking Talents requires NP, which can be obtained by exchanging Cats or Talent Orbs in Storage after Into the Future Chapter 3 has been completed. The amount of NP awarded is dependent on the item's rarity, with rarer items being worth more NP. However, merging D-grade Talent Orbs into a higher grade always results in a significant loss in NP value.

